   the odd sense that you are refering to it, positive sum.

No, in the sense that *you* are referring to it (total population), it
is positive sum.  In the sense that *I* am referring to it (fraction
of the gene pool), it is zero sum.  Since we are measuring the
outcomes in different (sometimes strongly different) ways, it is not
surprising that we get different answers.

The subtle consequence of this is that we can derive two conclusions,
which give different information:

- Those genes which are good at maximizing the fraction of the gene
pool they possess will tend to possess the largest fracton of the gene
pool.

- Those genes which are good at maximizing the number of organisms
that they possess will tend to possess the largest number of
organisms.

Dale

